{"updated":"2026-09-05","methodology":{"note":"V3.1 keeps raw capital/activity observations separate from strategic scores, adds geography and time-horizon context, evidence-derived confidence, driver-based scenarios, rank robustness, live hero anchors, immutable history, change-only publishing, and a review-gated source-discovery workflow. Cross-sector money measures remain intentionally non-comparable.","defaultWeights":{"capital":12,"capitalQuality":6,"momentum":10,"durability":11,"scarcity":9,"income":8,"aiResilience":8,"businessValue":9,"entrepreneurship":6,"defensibility":6,"accessibility":4,"proofability":3,"valueCapture":6,"transferability":4,"optionality":2,"hypeRisk":6,"crowdingRisk":6},"formulas":{"Overall Opportunity":"Weighted average of positive dimensions minus a hype-risk penalty. User adjustable.","Market Attractiveness":"Capital, momentum, durability, business value, defensibility, value capture, entrepreneurship and confidence, with hype penalty.","Career Attractiveness":"Income, scarcity, AI resilience, business value, transferability, optionality, accessibility, value capture and durability.","Personal Fit":"If no preference dimensions are activated, Personal Fit equals Career Attractiveness. Active preferences contribute a weighted intensity-match component; untouched sliders contribute zero information.","Context adjustment":"Selected objective is blended with geography (10%) and selected time-horizon thesis (15%); the underlying objective remains 75%.","Confidence":"Calculated from source quality, source count, source diversity, recency and evidence directness for the exact opportunity node.","Robustness":"Monte Carlo simulation perturbs evidence-based scores according to confidence; Overall Opportunity also perturbs user weights. Output is Top-5 probability, median rank and 10–90% rank range."},"rawCapitalRule":"Raw capital observations are displayed with their flow type and status. They are not summed or ranked directly across unlike categories such as government expenditure, technology spending, industry sales, VC/M&A, or cumulative infrastructure requirements."},"sources":[{"id":"S1","name":"Gartner — Worldwide AI Spending 2026","date":"2026-05-19","url":"https://www.gartner.com/en/newsroom/press-releases/2026-05-19-gartner-forecasts-worldwide-ai-spending-to-grow-47-percent-in-2026","note":"AI infrastructure $1.431T; AI services $585.5B; AI software $453.2B in 2026.","category":"Market research","qualityScore":88,"directness":"Forecast + vendor/market model"},{"id":"S2","name":"IEA — Key Questions on Energy and AI","date":"2026","url":"https://www.iea.org/reports/key-questions-on-energy-and-ai/executive-summary","note":"Capex of five major tech companies exceeded $400B in 2025 and is expected to rise 75% in 2026.","category":"Intergovernmental","qualityScore":95,"directness":"Observed corporate capex + forecast"},{"id":"S3","name":"McKinsey — $7T data-center build-out","date":"2026-03-27","url":"https://www.mckinsey.com/industries/technology-media-and-telecommunications/our-insights/the-7-trillion-dollar-data-center-build-out-how-industrials-can-capture-their-share","note":"Global data-center spending could reach about $7T through 2030; power and thermal equipment are constraints.","category":"Consulting research","qualityScore":82,"directness":"Scenario / cumulative investment estimate"},{"id":"S4","name":"Gartner — IT Spending 2026","date":"2026-07-27","url":"https://www.gartner.com/en/newsroom/press-releases/2026-07-27-gartner-forecasts-worldwide-it-spending-to-grow-14-point-2-percent-in-2026-totaling-6-point-37-trillion","note":"Worldwide IT spending forecast $6.37T in 2026; data centers and IaaS among major growth drivers.","category":"Market research","qualityScore":88,"directness":"Market-spend forecast"},{"id":"S5","name":"Gartner — Information Security 2026","date":"2026-02-05","url":"https://www.gartner.com/en/documents/7408930","note":"Information-security spending expected to reach $244B in 2026, +11.6%.","category":"Market research","qualityScore":88,"directness":"Market-spend forecast"},{"id":"S6","name":"SIA — Global Semiconductor Sales 2025 / 2026 outlook","date":"2026-02-06","url":"https://www.semiconductors.org/global-annual-semiconductor-sales-increase-25-6-to-791-7-billion-in-2025/","note":"Global semiconductor sales were $630.5B in 2024 and $791.7B in 2025 (+25.6%); SIA said 2026 sales were projected to reach roughly $1T.","category":"Industry association","qualityScore":92,"directness":"Observed sales + industry forecast"},{"id":"S7","name":"SIPRI — World Military Expenditure 2025","date":"2026-04-27","url":"https://www.sipri.org/media/press-release/2026/global-military-spending-rise-continues-european-and-asian-expenditures-surge","note":"World military expenditure $2.887T in 2025, +2.9% real; Europe +14%.","category":"Independent institute","qualityScore":96,"directness":"Observed government expenditure"},{"id":"S8","name":"Dealroom/NATO Innovation Fund — European Defence, Security & Resilience","date":"2026-02-10","url":"https://dealroom.co/reports/defence-security-and-resilience-in-europe-2026","note":"European defence/security/resilience startups raised record $8.7B VC in 2025, +55%.","category":"Market-data platform","qualityScore":84,"directness":"Observed venture funding"},{"id":"S9","name":"IFR — World Robotics 2025","date":"2025-09-25","url":"https://ifr.org/worldrobotics/report-2025","note":"542,000 industrial robots installed globally in 2024, more than double ten years earlier.","category":"Industry federation","qualityScore":92,"directness":"Observed installations"},{"id":"S10","name":"IFR — US Robot Industry 2026 update","date":"2026-06-18","url":"https://ifr.org/ifr-press-releases/en/news/","note":"US industrial robot installations rose 11% year over year to 38,000 in 2025.","category":"Industry federation","qualityScore":92,"directness":"Observed installations"},{"id":"S11","name":"IEA — World Energy Investment 2026","date":"2026-05-28","url":"https://www.iea.org/reports/world-energy-investment-2026","note":"Global energy investment expected at record $3.4T in 2026, +5%; about $2.2T into clean energy.","category":"Intergovernmental","qualityScore":97,"directness":"Investment estimate / forecast"},{"id":"S12","name":"McKinsey — Global Infrastructure Report 2026","date":"2026-03-23","url":"https://www.mckinsey.com/industries/private-capital/our-insights/global-private-markets-report/infrastructure","note":"$106T global infrastructure investment need through 2040; record ~$200B infrastructure fundraising in 2025.","category":"Consulting research","qualityScore":82,"directness":"Long-run infrastructure requirement + fundraising"},{"id":"S13","name":"KPMG — Venture Pulse Q2 2026","date":"2026-07-23","url":"https://kpmg.com/xx/en/media/press-releases/2026/07/vc-investment-already-at-five-year-high-of-billions.html","note":"Global VC $227.4B in Q2 2026; $560.4B year-to-date at mid-year, driven by mega AI rounds.","category":"Professional services","qualityScore":82,"directness":"Observed / reported venture investment"},{"id":"S14","name":"KPMG — Pulse of Fintech H1 2026","date":"2026-09","url":"https://kpmg.com/cy/en/insights/2026/09/pulse-of-fintech.html","note":"Global fintech investment $103.1B in H1 2026 vs $72.2B H2 2025; VC $31.5B.","category":"Professional services","qualityScore":84,"directness":"Observed / reported fintech investment"},{"id":"S15","name":"EY — Biotech Beyond Borders 2026","date":"2026-06-09","url":"https://www.ey.com/en_us/newsroom/2026/06/ey-2026-biotech-beyond-borders-report-a-fundamentally-strong-biotech-industry-seeks-balance-amid-continued-uncertainty","note":"Biotech financing $68.5B in 2025, +11%; Q1 2026 M&A value $36B.","category":"Professional services","qualityScore":82,"directness":"Observed / reported biotech financing"},{"id":"S16","name":"SVB — H2 2026 Healthcare Industry Trends","date":"2026-H2","url":"https://www.svb.com/trends-insights/reports/healthcare-investments-and-exits/","note":"Biopharma VC funding $12.6B in H1 2026; 25 private acquisitions in H1.","category":"Financial institution research","qualityScore":78,"directness":"Observed / reported healthcare financing"},{"id":"S17","name":"WEF — Future of Jobs Report 2025","date":"2025-01","url":"https://www.weforum.org/publications/the-future-of-jobs-report-2025/digest/","note":"AI/big data and networks/cybersecurity are the fastest-growing skills; robotics and energy systems are major transformation drivers.","category":"Multistakeholder institution","qualityScore":80,"directness":"Employer survey / structural labor trends"},{"id":"S18","name":"Dealroom — European Deep Tech Report 2026","date":"2026-03-24","url":"https://dealroom.co/reports/the-european-deep-tech-report-2026","note":"Deep tech reached 32% of European VC in 2025; Europe $20B (+21%), US $144B (+92%).","category":"Market-data platform","qualityScore":84,"directness":"Observed venture funding"},{"id":"S19","name":"Gartner — AI-optimized IaaS 2026","date":"2026-08-10","url":"https://www.gartner.com/en/newsroom/press-releases/2026-08-10-gartner-forecasts-worldwide-artificial-intelligence-optimized-iaas-spending-to-grow-96-percent-in-2026","note":"AI-optimized IaaS spending forecast $42B in 2026, +96%.","category":"Market research","qualityScore":88,"directness":"Market-spend forecast"},{"id":"S20","name":"Gartner — Agentic AI and Enterprise Software","date":"2026-07-01","url":"https://www.gartner.com/en/newsroom/press-releases/2026-07-01-gartner-says-us-dollars-234-billion-in-enterprise-application-software-spend-is-at-risk-from-agentic-artificial-intelligence","note":"Up to $234B of enterprise application spend exposed to agentic arbitrage by 2030.","category":"Market research","qualityScore":84,"directness":"Scenario / forecast"},{"id":"S21","name":"SIPRI — World Military Expenditure 2024","date":"2025-04","url":"https://www.sipri.org/publications/2025/sipri-fact-sheets/trends-world-military-expenditure-2024","note":"World military expenditure reached $2.718T in 2024, +9.4% in real terms.","category":"Independent institute","qualityScore":96,"directness":"Observed government expenditure"},{"id":"S22","name":"IEA — World Energy Investment 2025","date":"2025-06-05","url":"https://www.iea.org/reports/world-energy-investment-2025/executive-summary","note":"Global energy investment was set to reach $3.3T in 2025, +2% in real terms on 2024; about $2.2T to clean energy.","category":"Intergovernmental","qualityScore":97,"directness":"Investment estimate / forecast"},{"id":"S23","name":"SIA — WSTS Spring 2026 semiconductor forecast","date":"2026-06-05","url":"https://www.semiconductors.org/global-semiconductor-sales-increase-11-month-to-month-in-april/","note":"SIA endorsed the WSTS Spring 2026 forecast projecting annual global semiconductor sales above $1.5T in 2026 and $1.9T in 2027.","category":"Industry association / market data","qualityScore":92,"directness":95},{"id":"S24","name":"SIA — July 2026 global semiconductor sales","date":"2026-09-04","url":"https://www.semiconductors.org/global-semiconductor-sales-increase-6-4-month-to-month-in-july/","note":"SIA reported $146.8B in July 2026 global semiconductor sales, up 135.1% year over year; year-to-date sales through July exceeded the prior full-year record.","category":"Industry association / market data","qualityScore":92,"directness":98}],"nodes":[{"id":"ai-infra","name":"AI Infrastructure & Inference Systems","sector":"AI / Compute","thesis":"The strongest pure-tech capital wave: the bottleneck shifts from model novelty toward reliable, efficient inference, serving, orchestration and cost control.","evidence":"$1.43T 2026 AI-infrastructure spend; major tech capex is accelerating and enterprise AI usage is moving into production.","sources":["S1","S2","S19"],"scores":{"capital":98,"momentum":99,"durability":90,"scarcity":90,"income":98,"aiResilience":95,"businessValue":97,"entrepreneurship":84,"defens